==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=polar}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|LL.|en}} '''[[polaris|polāris]]'''

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpəʊ̯lə(ɹ)/|[ˈpʰəʊ̯lə(ɹ)]}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpoʊ̯lɚ/|[ˈpʰoʊ̯lɚ]}}
* {{rhymes|əʊlə(ɹ)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# of, relating to, measured from, or referred to a [[geographic]] [[pole]] (the [[North Pole]] or [[South Pole]])
# of an [[orbit]] that passes over, or near, one of these poles
# {{context|chemistry|lang=en}} having a [[dipole]]; [[ionic]]
# {{context|mathematics|lang=en}} of a [[coordinate]] [[system]], specifying the [[location]] of a [[point]] in a [[plane]] by using a [[radius]] and an [[angle]]
# {{context|linguistics|of a [[question]]|lang=en}} Having but [[two]] possible [[answer]]s, ''[[yes]]'' and ''[[no]]''.

